<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Josiah Martin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1737–1786</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josiah">Josiah</a> Martin was a British army officer and the last royal governor of North Carolina, serving from 1771. As revolutionary committees took control, he fled to a British warship in 1775, and he encouraged the Loyalist rising that was defeated at Moore's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> Bridge in February 1776. He later served with the British army in the southern campaigns.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/josiah-martin.jpg" alt="Josiah Martin" width="320" height="449" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jeremiah Meyer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Josiah_Martin_(1737%E2%80%931786)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
